      "extract": "We quickly sketch some background on modular curves; for fuller details the reader may want to consult [Deligne and Rapoport 1973; Freitas et al. 2015, Section 2.2.2; Rohrlich 1997]. Let H∗= H ∪Q ∪{∞} denote the extended upper half-plane. The modular group SL2(Z) acts on H by fractional linear transformations. The quotient SL2(Z)\\H∗is a compact Riemann surface of genus 0, and hence is the analytiﬁcation of a genus 0",
